WEBVTT

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.580
Hey, is it alright for us to stay like this?

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.080
Weren't we much more enthusiastic in the past?

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.350
Be it Yatabe, Tsukuba or the streets,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.580
we used to strive to produce the highest speed figures.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:54.990
So what? BlackBird has Kitami.
R32 has Yamamoto, Yatabe has Ohta.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.590
They are all old-timers.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.100
That's true.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.450
Let's do this!

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:03.320
Interesting!

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:07.100
Alright, let's try aiming for that R32 first.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.600
<i>What's with the car coming up from behind? Overtaking like this?</i>

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.610
<i>No. It's not overtaking. Then what? It's catching up to me?</i>

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.220
<i>Just exactly how fast is this car driving?</i>

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.930
Did I miss the meeting time?

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:55.600
Even after ditching my busy job for two weeks.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.940
It's been a while since I've come out here.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.950
I won't be able to meet him...

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:12.010
That was fast! You were driving at a remarkable speed.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:15.250
I never thought there was a car that could catch up to me.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.250
Do you mind if I look at the engine?

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.210
Sure, go ahead.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:26.700
A L-Type Twin Turbo. I see, the L is a down-flow type.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.380
Looks like you have an amazing turbine in there too.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:30.690
I couldn't catch up.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.500
You entered Wangan via the Rainbow Bridge, right?

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.710
When your car suddenly entered my line of sight,

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.490
I thought, "Ah, that car is skilled".

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.310
I felt that your drive style is like mine.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:47.950
So I went all out and accelerated.
I couldn't close the distance at all.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.910
As for me, I absolutely didn't notice you at all.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.450
You decelerated just before the Tsubasa Bridge, right?

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:54.960
It was then I finally caught up with you.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.180
Is that so? I'm glad.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.830
I don't stand even the slightest chance against you.

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:03.130
Akio-kun. Akio-kun!

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.340
Reina.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.110
I'm glad, we finally could meet.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.510
You... are the one from just now.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.100
So, you were originally chasing Reina's R?

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.680
She disappeared too easily though.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:16.800
Where's your R, Reina?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.320
Mine is-

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.840
I'll charge them a great deal more later.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.840
This isn't really my day. Well, looks like I should be able to go back.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.840
On its own? You mustn't do that.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.830
But it's only this much...

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.100
You definitely can't! Call a tow truck to pick it up.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.800
How troublesome, to be called out at this time of the day.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.200
<i>This R, it's from Yamamoto Speed!</i>

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.330
I'm deeply impressed, the boss came personally.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.270
Well, you did called my house directly.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.560
Thanks.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.080
This is horrible. It can't go on its own.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.340
But it doesn't look that bad to me.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.670
The wheel was hit, right?

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:22.050
In this situation, it could have knocked the arm section.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.330
It will be a little shaky if you drive, but should be fine.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:30.100
However, that kind of judgment will only
cause permanent damage on the car.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.150
I'm glad I did as you told me.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.060
Nice to meet you, Yamamoto-san. I am...

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.100
I know. Kuroki-kun from Flat Racing, right?

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.680
Is this R yours?

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:43.360
Yes.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.320
It looks fast and has a certain air about it.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:49.840
Just a while ago, I wasn't able to catch up to her R at all.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.990
I was also chased by the Z.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.580
Sorry that I'm your rival.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.770
I'm restarting what I did last time,

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:00.290
and thought I had already graduated from tuning...

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.550
Why did you resume this work?

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.760
I wonder why...

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.020
It's a little unbalanced.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.780
Shall I take a look? I'll reset it in 5 minutes.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.690
You know him, right? This guy.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.850
I know a little about Takagi-san.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.990
If I'm right, he did the settings for the Supra.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:39.250
That's right, also know as "Jetting of Tominaga".
The devil of computer settings.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.770
The devil's you, Kitami-san.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:48.350
I wanted to ask you about it once, why
do you keep driving only the Porsche?

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.690
There are other good cars too.

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:54.260
Good cars. Like the GT-R?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.190
Yes. It's awesome, the R.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:01.790
In Shutokou Area which includes Wangan,
there's no other machine above it.

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.720
Anyway, the Porsche is too heavy to be used.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.380
At high speeds, the front is lifted and

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.240
the front tire's contact patch loses feel.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:09.610
So what?

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.740
They are what's important.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:19.850
The car as a machine and myself as
a human, both properly engaged,

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:24.500
truly racing with my life on the line,
truly completing until the end.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.180
Furthermore, in the event that the worst happened,

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:30.000
the car is just thought to be of no more use.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.460
Is that what is important?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.160
That's right, it's as you said it.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:41.230
But even so, as a machine, it's better that the potential is higher.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.980
Kitami-san, will you let me do it?

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:50.440
The settings of this Porsche, which is
disadvantageous compared to the R,

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.700
and also another one, the Z, which is even
more disadvantageous than this Porsche.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:12.190
Yo, Taka. I brought you the stuff I promised.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:14.190
Thanks for coming all the way.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:16.600
You're really working by yourself in the factory.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.550
It's more relaxing this way.

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:21.330
You tune only Rs now!

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:24.460
Well, since I'm on my own, if it's possible

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.110
I don't want to touch trivial cars anymore.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:30.570
If you say that, your factory will surely
be closed down, you know. Here you go.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.110
Thanks.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:34.080
Why are you interested in L-types?

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.760
Since you only handle Rs.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.390
Just something personal.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:39.070
It won't make you any money.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.880
Actually, I met a fully-loaded L-type, an insanely fast Z.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.050
A Z?

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:49.120
It felt like a slap in the face.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:56.640
Lya-san, what do you think of the R200 club lately?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:02.600
I felt that we used to aim higher.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:07.270
200mph on the Yatabe course, a gathering of tuners who could dish out 320km/h,

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.070
having pride in R200 Club's name.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:14.320
Lately, it's only been about financial
issues, like how much profit is earned.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.820
That's true, but that's reality.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.760
After all, a tuner is the end of rider.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.140
After all that effort handling time and money,

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.660
once you realize there's no turning back,

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:29.520
this time I want to recover both
and turn back to the other side.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.090
Don't dwell too much into earning money.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.090
By doing what you like, isn't that good enough?

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:41.430
The person who gave me that piece of
scrap, do you know what he's doing now?

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.830
In a bar.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:48.310
He's like you in a way, always serious
and never allowing compromises.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.560
The first reason why a tuner would go out of business,

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.570
would be because he brought destruction upon himself.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.900
Distancing himself from his own customers,

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.060
just like what you're doing now.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:01.610
I'm now following Motoki's group,

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:04.580
because I want to keep on living in this world.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:07.580
It's easy to ruin yourself, Taka.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:14.090
I'll say just one thing, we are not just only counting money.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:19.060
We're aiming for the BlackBird and the rumored white R32.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:24.520
We plan to show those old aged tuners
what we can do. And maybe even that Z.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:35.860
That's Yamamoto-san. How young, still in his twenties.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:39.970
Known for being a radical, Yamamoto
always came to Yatabe with his Blue.

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:45.170
The first one to go around 10000 with an L was Yamamoto.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.170
Ohta-san did it too, with the L.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:55.190
It's all here, the famous places from everywhere in here.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.590
Kitami Jun.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:02.340
Although he didn't appear in the magazine's event or the Yatabe Try,

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.850
as expected, Kitami Jun is the best with the L.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:10.400
Because he was fast, he entered the Try with an L28 Custom 3.0.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:15.510
Twin turbo using unconventional settings and repeated the "Buro".

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.860
And then in the end, he created the Devil Z.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:23.490
Devil Z?

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.200
Is that...

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.180
The turbo kicks in at 6000rpm in fourth gear.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:44.680
Ok.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.900
In any case, it's great that you personally sat in the car.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.190
Not at all, as expected of a car from you, Kitami-san.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.930
However, it's made really well.

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:04.730
I've done quite a number of settings for Flat 6 Engines,

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.990
but this is a first for this level of work.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.910
For you, you should be able to put together this level of work now.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:15.700
You gotta be kidding, no way.
I only run an ordinary computer shop.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.960
But I don't understand.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.680
Why did someone like you who is so
difficult become crazy over that guy?

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.370
Putting the inexperienced Yamamoto aside,

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.500
that Takagi and Ohta, and even the other guys,,

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:32.600
all completely became interested in this.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:36.350
Indeed, why is it? Say, Kitami-san.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:44.860
I'm sorry, sir. We're closing already.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:48.950
Koyama-san, right? I came after asking about you from Yasu-san.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:49.860
Yasu?

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:52.870
Yes. I borrowed the L-Type engine's scrap from you.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.100
I did make that in the past.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:58.840
Is that yours?

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.050
Yes.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.190
Can I have a quick look at it?

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:04.550
If you want to talk about cars, it's gotta start from there.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.820
It must have been tough, to have reached this level.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.070
That's right, it took me a total of 6 years.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:20.820
6 years, huh? What great skills.
I roughly understand, people like you.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.940
I have something I would like to ask you.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.120
What is it?

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.030
Recently, I drove at 300km/h on Tsubasa Bridge.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:31.450
It's possible, if it's this car.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.540
And there was an S30Z that was chasing me.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:35.790
Z?

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.040
Could that be the Devil Z?

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:53.470
I see, it's a great car. A GT-R, it's just like the rumors.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.980
For the sake of this car, I have been
working nonstop from morning until night.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:07.770
Not having the time to drive my prized
R, in a time when I was in a real fix,

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:09.800
I met someone called Tominaga-san.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.890
It's enough, I'll read about it later.

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.090
Do you know him? Tominaga-san?

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:16.960
When I was installing the carburetor turbo, he was a great help.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.340
Even until now, the demo cars in fast car shops

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:21.240
are mostly tuned by Tominaga-san, right?

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.100
What's wrong?

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.210
It's the Z.

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:30.720
That's the Z that chased me on the Tsubasa Bridge.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.180
<i>Such a young man driving the Z?!</i>

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:46.650
I was looking for you, thinking that you might be here.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:49.750
I'm glad. This is Koyama-san.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.360
He's considerably knowledgeable about L-type engines.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:55.690
Hey, hey, that's already in the past.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:58.160
I'm Asakura Akio. Nice to meet you.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.420
You're young. University student?

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:03.350
No, I couldn't graduate from high school.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.920
Those into cars are all like that.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.430
Well, since we're done with self-introductions, let's go for a run.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:13.420
That's fine, let's go all out.

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:15.140
Alright, it's a challenge!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.280
I'm kidding, kidding.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:18.390
Let's just go normally.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.600
Ok, let's go normally then.

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:30.930
What do you think, Koyama-san? That's the Devil Z, right?

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:31.610
Probably.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:37.120
Because it's a phantom car that we
know races, but have never seen before.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.620
I'll let him have the first attack.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.050
<i>W-What a car...</i>

00:15:56.340 --> 00:16:00.080
<i>It's not that Kitami didn't do anything special.</i>

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:05.980
<i>However, it's that the Z is running with a will of its own.</i>

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:09.820
<i>This powerful presence which ignores its surroundings.</i>

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.050
The surrounding air is trembling.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.690
When I was still at my peak,

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:16.690
I could never meet it even when I really wanted to.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.630
Reina-chan, you still driving the GT-R?

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.890
Yes, it's a good car. I won't cheat on it.

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:33.250
Why don't you drive a more fashionable car once in a while?

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:36.090
Well then, what would you recommend, Kijima-san?

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:38.980
How about a '69 Dodge Challenger?

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:40.780
But nobody knows it.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.450
Then until next time.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.460
Goodbye.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.860
Drive Go Go!

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.860
Ok, thank you for your hard work!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.810
Thank you.

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:56.360
Thanks for your work.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.870
By the way, Reina-chan, I heard a strange rumor.

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:05.420
Do you know about the group of
tuners which did 320km/h on Yatabe,

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.500
gathered and formed the R200 Club?

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:09.410
R200?

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:17.970
Those guys are aiming at your GT-R. It's not only you.

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:19.770
Reina-chan, you don't know?

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.450
It seems the fast cars on Shutokou,

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:24.970
BlackBird and that Z have also been targeted.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.000
In any case, it's better if you be careful.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:33.930
Boss!

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:40.530
Hey, I'm working on it.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:43.570
It still takes some time to fix even
if it's just a depression in the fender.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:48.000
Well actually, this time I changed
the settings for the wheels slightly.

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:49.250
You changed it?

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:52.200
It'll cause a little under-steer,

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.760
but in exchange, at high speeds it's much more stable.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.250
Boss...

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:59.040
Well, there's a lot of strange rumors floating around.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:03.370
I'm not really worried about it. You bought an R34?

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:05.220
It's a demo car.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.380
Since I went back to my old name,

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:09.730
I thought about dabbling in it once again.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:12.490
So you also prefer this.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.200
Tominaga-san wants to change the Z's settings?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:22.030
I can't do a thing since he wants to do it.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.430
Is it a nuisance, Akio?

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:26.710
No , not at all. If it's Tominaga-san
doing it then I couldn't ask for more.

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:29.120
The changes will be astonishing.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.940
He's a disagreeable guy, but no one
can top him when it comes to settings.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.720
If it's a disagreeable person, that goes for you too, Kitami-san.

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:39.220
Might as well discard that old carburetor
and convert it to use fuel injection!

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:40.860
That's good.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:44.850
After throttling for 6 years, the surge tank's
efficiency has to be properly reconfigured.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.220
That'll output a lot of power.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.930
By all means, I'll leave the Z's settings in your hands.

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.490
But if possible, I'd like to retain the carburetor,

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:54.530
and also leave the power as it is.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:55.480
Even the power?

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:56.740
Yes.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:09.660
That's careless of you, to leave your factory wide open.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:18.530
The 32, 33 and 34. In truth, the R has already reached a limit,

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:21.530
tension has been continuously dropping recently.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:24.890
And the 04 or Yatabe Try also did not motivate me at all,

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.650
and I was afraid to be dropped.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:31.190
But, feeling like I've seen the light all of a sudden,

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.610
it's a shock to me.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:37.380
I didn't know at all. That kind of car actually existed...

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:38.150
That would be?

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.640
An L28 Custom Twin Turbo.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:45.650
To dethrone that Z known as the Devil, it's gotta be the GT-R, right?

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:50.370
I understand. But as for the white R32, leave it alone.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.180
White R32?

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.860
Well then, I only came here to say that.

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:01.530
<i>Shima-sensei from the 2nd Surgical Department.</i>

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:05.130
<i>there's a guest in the 1st Floor Lobby for you.</i>

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:07.830
You've finished already?

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:11.730
Perfectly. I didn't just do a sloppy overnight job,

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.850
but well, you understand how it's like when you
unintentionally get hooked up on something, right?

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:20.810
But as a doctor, you're really raking in a profit, huh.

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.860
At your age, you can leisurely drive this kind of car.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.380
You've probably rode your colleagues' fancy cars too, right?

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:27.630
That's not true.

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:30.370
You're the only special one? How come?

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.090
It's simple. Because I spend all money for this purpose.

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:34.550
All?

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:38.720
A young guy working at a stand, even
if his earn barely enough for a living,

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:43.500
might still put in a lot of money for
car modifications, right? It's the same.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:46.500
They spend all income for that purpose.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:51.910
Now I see. I kind of understand why Kitami-san is so fond of you.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:55.570
He actually hates people like you, that guy.

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:57.240
He's fond of me?

00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:59.180
Well, pretty much.

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:03.360
I really don't understand.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:06.810
I can understand it if it's an old person which
has been brought up with the use of carburetors,

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:09.270
but why are you from the present time
so particular about it to this extent?

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:11.210
It's not about being fussy.

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:15.830
It's just that, with just the new settings, I feel
that it's already good enough in its current state.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:19.710
No, if I continue driving it, I feel that
it can reach a considerably higher level.

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:23.620
But, just by changing the carburetor,

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:25.250
it definitely won't feel like this Z anymore.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.910
Which means you want nothing changed
and everything left the way it is.

00:21:27.910 --> 00:21:28.800
If possible.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:33.170
Even though you both are equally fast,
you are totally different from him.

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:39.940
That guy, will only see the BlackBird
as a machine. That is his strength.

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:43.040
You are too kind-hearted. Whether it's good or bad,

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.790
when you handle a machine, you put in too much of your emotions.

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:49.170
But that contributes to both your speed and weakness.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:56.870
The car's condition looks good.

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:59.080
I'm Kuroki from Flat Racing.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.840
From the R200 Club?

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:03.910
As of this moment, I'm still.

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:06.840
Are you heading towards Tokyo now? If you don't mind, wanna race?

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:11.620
That's fine with me. I was just looking
for someone to race with. The course?

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:15.680
Going uphill at Yokohane, joining
Wangan from Shouwajima junction.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:17.270
I get it.

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:20.820
It's just a coincidence since we're talking
about Yokohane, but do you know?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:24.070
It's the best course of the guy with the Z.

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.370
The other stages aside,

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:29.790
if it's Yokohane, I doubt you can catch up to him there.

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:30.720
Myself too.

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:43.500
<i>I don't hate Yokohane.</i>

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:48.030
<i>The road is uneven, the lanes are narrow
and the speed is more than I imagined.</i>

00:22:48.030 --> 00:22:50.940
<i>Deception won't work against his car or skill.</i>

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:58.140
<i>He's good and he's not only good...</i>

00:22:58.140 --> 00:22:59.850
<i>Such speed...</i>

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:06.600
<i>I can't catch up, whether it's that Z or this BlackBird.</i>

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:08.820
<i>Such people actually exist...</i>

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:12.320
<i>I'll have to redo everything from square one.</i>

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.040
<i>Fine, I'll do it!</i>

00:23:14.540 --> 00:23:18.200
<i>If I just lose out now, then it won't be
possible for me to give up on this world.</i>
